# Product Hub changes workflow

## Prefer .md over Jira API when reading

When you need **Product Hub content** (user story text, subtask summaries, descriptions, status, assignee, acceptance criteria):

1. **Search or read the .md files first** in `docs/product-hub-jira/` (e.g. by epic folder and `[US-x.y]: …` files). Assume they are in sync with Jira.
2. **Call the Jira API only when** the .md doesn’t have what you need, or when you must **perform an action** (create issue, update, assign, transition, etc.).

This saves resources and keeps work local when the .md is the source of truth.

---

When the user asks to **change** something in Product Hub (user stories, subtasks, acceptance criteria, story text, etc.):

1. **Edit the .md files first**  
   Make all changes in `docs/product-hub-jira/` — update the relevant epic folder and .md file(s). Do not update Jira via the API yet.

2. **List the changes and ask for confirmation**  
   Summarise what you changed (file paths, what was added/removed/edited) and ask: **"Confirm if you want these changes synced to Jira."**

3. **Sync to Jira only after confirmation**  
   If the user confirms, use the Jira API script (`scripts/jira-api.mjs` update, or other scripts as needed) to apply the same changes to Jira so that Jira matches the .md.

**.md is the source of truth for edits**; Jira is updated only after the user confirms.

When the user asks to **sync** or **pull** from Jira (e.g. "sync the .md with Jira"), run the sync scripts to update the .md from Jira — no confirmation needed for that direction.
